  "engine": "trombone world · one N-D body",
  "note": "The 36 notes of the repository's trombone solo, tongued, slurred and smeared, with scoops, swells, vibrato, a rip up to C5 and two falls, played by one Ariadne World: a single body whose bore is a network of tubes, whose slide is the body's one coordinate and whose lips are the runtime's flow valve, blown from the lungs. Measured on this render, every note sounds on the partial the player placed it on (36 of 36), a median of 5.7 cents from the written pitch and 13.7 at most, and sustained notes written at the same dynamic spread over a median of 0.7 dB; the ledger closes to 3.6e-15 in its worst frame. It does not brighten as it gets louder: the runtime's acoustics are linear, so nothing steepens the wave in the bore. Heard dry, with no room.",
